{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/151494-music-recommendations-for-ic-werewolf-game-set-in-the-90s","id":151494,"title":"Music Recommendations for IC Werewolf game set in the 90s","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-28T11:19:26-07:00","id":151494,"title":"Music Recommendations for IC Werewolf game set in the 90s","content":"I'm starting to lay the groundwork for a Werewolf game that I'll be running once Idigam Chronicles comes out. I know that it'll be set in the Washington state/British Columbia area in the early-to-mid-1990s.<br /> <br /> I've started using music in my 80s Seattle Vampire game, but I don't know 90s music near as well as I know 80s music. Could somebody make some recommendations that they think screams &quot;90s&quot; as well as Werewolf? Or even just bitchin' 90s music. I'm open to many ideas. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T02:29:15-07:00","id":153626,"title":"","content":"Look into Nirvana, Pearl jam, and Soundgarden for the Grunge craze. Hole, Bikini Kill, The Raincoats, for the Riot Grrl Movement. Anthrax, Biohazard, and Metallica for Thrash.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Forgot Danzig, Weezer, Red Hot Chili Peppers, Smashing Pumpkins and Radio Head","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2861,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","user":"Nyx","date":". 05-30-2014, 05:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T04:57:12-07:00","id":153706,"title":"","content":"I'd been looking into Nirvana (which I never really <i>listened to</i>, man, I missed out), but completely forgot about the Riot Grrl and Thrash stuff.<br /> <br /> ASIDE: I've also been grateful for Stew's music links at the end of each blog. Seriously man, thanks for that. Not specifically 90s but it's some good stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0